WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.640
A FILM BY PAUL URKIJO ALIJO

3
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.080
Fear the night.

4
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.600
The night. a place rife with blasphemy.

5
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.360
refuge of terrible creatures

6
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.600
that escape the light of God.

7
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.120
The night gathers in
its bosom. perverse demons.

8
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.000
wicked witches. dark tales

9
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.680
which we shall now hear.

10
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.200
In the hour of darkness.

11
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.280
The good Christian sleeps in peace.

12
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.120
With the dawn.
the sun's rays will rise -

13
00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.520
light to guide us along
the path of the Lord.

14
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.080
And yet. so they say.

15
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.480
if the night should overtake you. flee -

16
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.840
and don't stray from the path home.

17
00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.560
or the darkness will swallow you...

18
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.480
forever.

19
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.800
But who would stray from the path?

20
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.680
Who would abandon the light?

21
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.040
As the saying goes:

22
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.800
"The day belongs to those of the day."

23
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.400
and as the wind whispers:

24
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.600
"The night to those of the night."

25
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:49.960
THE NIGHT

26
00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.800
You... are to blame...

27
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.720
You... are to blame...

28
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.080
Kattalin.

29
00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.200
Why do you keep looking out the window?

30
00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.720
- The night will creep into your eyes.
- Can't you hear it?

31
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.640
It's probably a fox.

32
00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.520
No. it sounded like a whistle.

33
00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.160
I'm hungry.

34
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.440
Tomorrow I'm going to Urdazubi.

35
00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.280
To speak to abbot Fray León's
secretary about the orchard.

36
00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.560
Luck will finally smile on us.

37
00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.160
And Don Mateo?

38
00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.240
Has anything been heard of him?

39
00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.680
No one has seen the parish priest
since what happened at the church.

40
00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.400
It's been a week now.

41
00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.720
I hope he keeps what he promised me.

42
00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.840
Disgusting.
It needs salt.

43
00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.480
Then you cook.

44
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.640
Watch yourself. Katalina.
Show me some respect!

45
00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.040
You've embarrassed me enough
before the whole village.

46
00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.800
You wouldn't want to end up...

47
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.400
living under a bridge.

48
00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:09.560
Bread.

49
00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.760
Aren't you going to eat?

50
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.960
Why won't you speak to me?

51
00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.840
You are my wife!

52
00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:21.840
You see?

53
00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.000
It has no flavour.

54
00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.520
Tomorrow I have to look presentable.
Lay out my Sunday shirt.

55
00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.120
I'm going to bed.

56
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.320
I know these past weeks haven't been easy.

57
00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.640
But from now on. things will improve.

58
00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.640
You'll see.

59
00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.400
You're my wife.

60
00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.360
No!

61
00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.400
Why do you despise me?

62
00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.120
Because I'm a cripple?

63
00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.480
Look what you've done.

64
00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.880
Katta.

65
00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.000
Katti.

66
00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.720
My shirt!

67
00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.520
I need it for tomorrow!

68
00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.680
Calm down.

69
00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.560
It's all right.

70
00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.820
Can you clean it?

71
00:11:15.144 --> 00:11:16.144
Huh?

72
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.240
My belly.

73
00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.120
Katta!

74
00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:04.520
Come back here!

75
00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.160
Kattalin!

76
00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:14.560
Very well. This first tale
begins with an unfortunate

77
00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:19.640
young woman who entered the forest
when not a single ray of sun remained -

78
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.840
when the road of the Night Above begins.

79
00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.240
For he is the night itself -

80
00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.920
Gaueko.

81
00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.760
Whoever dares enter the night

82
00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.720
will be lost -

83
00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.680
the darkness will engulf him forever.

84
00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:46.440
For there dwells Gaueko.
lord of those who dwell in the shadows.

85
00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.400
His is not a kingdom for men.

86
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:56.280
What fate awaits those
who dare to enter the night?

87
00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:06.200
The night...

88
00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.240
Pello?

89
00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:27.960
Pello. is that you?

90
00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.760
The night...

91
00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.680
...for those of the night.

92
00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.760
The night...

93
00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:50.080
...for those of the night.

94
00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.120
The night for those of the night!

95
00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:33.040
The night...

96
00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:45.760
...for those of the night!

97
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:52.800
Who's there?

98
00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.360
Come here.

99
00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.440
Hey!

100
00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.320
What are you doing here. little brat?

101
00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.360
- She was spying on us.
- Reme!

102
00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.040
Let her breathe.

103
00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:06.600
Can't you see she's scared?

104
00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.840
Graxi. what do we do with her?

105
00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.480
The poor thing's lost.

106
00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.400
She doesn't look innocent.

107
00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:19.360
Let her speak - then we'll see.

108
00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:20.520
What are you doing here?

109
00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.240
- Answer!
- Reme!

110
00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.320
Let her talk.

111
00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.160
Poor little thing.

112
00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.000
Are you alright?

113
00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.120
You're Kattalin.

114
00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:45.840
Aren't you?

115
00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.800
I've seen you at mass.

116
00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:50.800
What are you doing here?

117
00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.720
I left home... and something
followed me here.

118
00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.640
It's all right.

119
00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.760
You're safe with us.

120
00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.000
And why were you out at night?
Problems at home?

121
00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:06.800
I was going to the washhouse with dirty clothes...
and they started chasing me.

122
00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.880
It is dangerous to walk through
the forest alone at night.

123
00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:12.440
It's full of vermin.

124
00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.480
And your clothes?

125
00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.760
I lost them.

126
00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:18.040
I don't believe you!

127
00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.400
Kattalin.

128
00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.800
you're the one who married
Pello Goienetxea last autumn. aren't you?

129
00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.400
Where are you from?

130
00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.040
From Landibar.

131
00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.560
You're far from home.

132
00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.160
And this?

133
00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.040
Is it yours?

134
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.560
It's my husband's shirt.

135
00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:50.280
And that stain?
An accident?

136
00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.880
Give it to me - I'll clean it.

137
00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:57.920
These stains don't come out easily.

138
00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.760
"Outside. a dove; at home. a wolf."

139
00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.760
It's no hour to be doing laundry.

140
00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.240
And you?

141
00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:39.880
We are Beltra. Remedios.
and I'm Graxiana.

142
00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:41.640
Or Graxi.

143
00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.640
We're not here to wash.

144
00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.560
We came to pretend we're washing.

145
00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.280
This is our time.

146
00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:54.960
- No men.
- No one to bother us.

147
00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.800
And no one says anything?

148
00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.760
They haven't the slightest idea.

149
00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.480
And we'd best make sure no one finds out.

150
00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.920
Here we do as we please.

151
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.520
Old by day and young by night.

152
00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.680
Things have been ugly lately.

153
00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.040
The abbot of Urdazubi
has forbidden gatherings

154
00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:25.600
and the parish priests and
bailiffs are watching us like hawks.

155
00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:32.480
Those inquisitors see witches under every stone.

156
00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:38.920
Just having a drink is enough
to be singled out and dragged away.

157
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.080
You can't trust anyone.

158
00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:43.640
- Here. take it.
- No. thanks.

159
00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:48.600
We pass the time trading village gossip.

160
00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.480
And telling ghost stories.

161
00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.840
I was just finishing telling
one when you turned up.

162
00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.400
You can join us -

163
00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.880
as long as you tell one afterwards.

164
00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:01.480
Unless you'd rather go home.

165
00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:03.600
I don't know any.

166
00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:08.520
Surely you know some frightening
tale you can tell us.

167
00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:11.240
Something about spirits -

168
00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.320
or witches.

169
00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.080
Do you believe in witches?

170
00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.440
Reme's a witch.

171
00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:22.240
I don't know.

172
00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:27.640
Careful. girl.

173
00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:32.400
You needn't believe in them -
 but you mustn't say they don't exist.

174
00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.800
Alright.
My turn.

175
00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:42.160
What I am about to tell you
is no tale.

176
00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:47.560
It happened a month ago
to someone from the village.

177
00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:52.440
To Eugenia. the seamstress's daughter.

178
00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:58.840
Eugenia herself told me.
and now I'll tell you.

179
00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:04.120
Now that it's my turn.

180
00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:07.600
Pay attention - or off you go!

181
00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:14.400
From what they said.
a witch had cast the evil eye on the girl

182
00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:17.040
and invoked an ancient demon.

183
00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:21.680
A dark and twisted being -

184
00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:25.800
born of sin and envy.

185
00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:30.480
An evil spirit: Inguma.

186
00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.560
In our villages there is
a belief in the "Etxejaun".

187
00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:56.880
the spirits of our ancestors.

188
00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:01.760
They are owed praise.
for they guard the house

189
00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.760
and the fortune of those who dwell within it.

190
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:15.440
This is how they work.

191
00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:18.920
so long as their descendants
do not trouble them —

192
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:23.800
and no one. through wicked arts.
disturbs their rest.

193
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:45.800
Give it to me. son.

194
00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:52.640
Antton...

195
00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:55.480
Don't worry. Maritxu.

196
00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.200
You're going to be cured.

197
00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.080
Pray with me. son.

198
00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:10.640
I believe in God. Almighty Father.

199
00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:13.720
creator of Heaven and Earth.

200
00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:17.800
And in Jesus Christ. his only son.

201
00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:22.760
our Lord.
who was conceived of the Holy Spirit.

202
00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:28.760
He was incarnated from the Virgin Mary.
He suffered under the power of Pontius Pilate.

203
00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:32.240
He was crucified. died and buried.

204
00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.040
Enough!

205
00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:39.400
He descended into hell...

206
00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:54.920
Witchcraft.

207
00:24:56.840 --> 00:25:00.240
Ohpo. dapa. map. map. drepe. Map. ripi.

208
00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:04.000
Propo. tepe. gepe. apa. Mapa. ripi. txupu.

209
00:25:05.120 --> 00:25:08.840
Ohpo. dapa. map. map. drepe. Map. ripi.

210
00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:12.600
Propo. tepe. gepe. apa. Mapa. ripi. txupu.

211
00:25:38.480 --> 00:25:39.680
Where are you going?

212
00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:41.480
Eugenia?

213
00:25:59.800 --> 00:26:01.320
I'm staying here.

214
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:03.360
Don't be long.

215
00:26:12.760 --> 00:26:14.040
Father Mateo.

216
00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:15.120
Katalina.

217
00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:17.920
How is Maritxu?

218
00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:19.680
It is in the hands of God.

219
00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:23.360
Or maybe she's already
in the devil's clutches.

220
00:26:26.840 --> 00:26:27.680
Excuse me.

221
00:26:36.600 --> 00:26:37.560
Eugenia.

222
00:26:38.480 --> 00:26:39.680
Eugenia. how is she?

223
00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:41.800
I don't know.

224
00:26:56.760 --> 00:26:57.880
Antton.

225
00:26:57.960 --> 00:26:58.840
Kattalin.

226
00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:06.960
I'm going to get more wormwood herbal teas.

227
00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:20.560
Your neck...

228
00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:25.560
Kattalin.

229
00:27:26.680 --> 00:27:27.640
Maritxu.

230
00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:30.320
You're going to be fine. okay?

231
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:31.880
Look.

232
00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:39.760
You're going to be fine.
You'll see.

233
00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:41.400
Yes.

234
00:27:42.640 --> 00:27:45.200
And we will go to the Bayonne pilgrimage.

235
00:27:47.120 --> 00:27:49.000
To dance and jump.

236
00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:50.960
Yes. we will go.

237
00:28:06.080 --> 00:28:06.960
Pater Mateo.

238
00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:29.320
Wasn't she forbidden
from approaching the village?

239
00:28:41.080 --> 00:28:42.040
It was her.

240
00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:02.840
Mother. is she going to be okay?

241
00:29:03.200 --> 00:29:04.480
I don't know. son.

242
00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:06.320
Will Maritxu go to hell?

243
00:29:06.400 --> 00:29:07.920
Don't say that!

244
00:29:08.280 --> 00:29:09.600
But what's wrong with her?

245
00:29:09.680 --> 00:29:10.760
I don't know!

246
00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:20.480
Maritxu.

247
00:29:21.440 --> 00:29:22.400
Maritxu.

248
00:29:26.600 --> 00:29:27.480
Maritxu.

249
00:29:28.120 --> 00:29:29.240
Maritxu!

250
00:29:29.320 --> 00:29:31.520
Maritxu!

251
00:29:39.600 --> 00:29:40.680
You...

252
00:29:41.480 --> 00:29:44.240
You are guilty.

253
00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:45.320
You!

254
00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:47.640
What are you talking about?
Maritxu. it's me.

255
00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:49.880
Harlot!
Get out of my house!

256
00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:51.320
Maritxu. it's me.

257
00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:52.600
Out!

258
00:29:57.880 --> 00:29:58.880
Maritxu.

259
00:29:59.800 --> 00:30:00.960
Maritxu. it's me.

260
00:30:02.520 --> 00:30:03.720
Go away.
Get out of here.

261
00:30:04.920 --> 00:30:06.640
- Maritxu. it's me.
- Out!

262
00:30:07.360 --> 00:30:08.840
- Maritxu!
- Out!

263
00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:18.920
Why does God punish us in this way?

264
00:31:21.960 --> 00:31:23.440
Can't we do anything?

265
00:31:32.920 --> 00:31:37.240
Antton. go ask old Esther
the herbalist for help.

266
00:31:37.760 --> 00:31:40.800
She knows Maritxu.
She will know what to do.

267
00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:45.080
But don't let anyone
see you talking to her.

268
00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:42.760
Antton. come here.

269
00:32:51.600 --> 00:32:52.920
Poor thing.

270
00:32:54.040 --> 00:32:59.880
A spirit is tormenting
your sister Maritxu. I am certain.

271
00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:08.840
Who was the last
to die in your house?

272
00:33:09.720 --> 00:33:10.840
Grandfather Inguma.

273
00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:12.680
A year ago.

274
00:33:12.760 --> 00:33:17.040
Could he be angry with
your sister for some reason?

275
00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:18.880
No.

276
00:33:19.600 --> 00:33:20.880
Maritxu is a saint.

277
00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:22.120
She's a good person.

278
00:33:22.840 --> 00:33:24.800
Grandfather loved her very much.

279
00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:29.960
How much did he love her?
How much?

280
00:33:31.080 --> 00:33:33.080
More than anything in the world.

281
00:33:35.800 --> 00:33:37.040
It could be him...

282
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:40.160
This is what you are going to do.

283
00:33:43.040 --> 00:33:48.840
Take this candle and wind it around
the effigy carved in rememberance
of your Grandfather.

284
00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:59.160
Once the candle is lit.
cover it with a bowl.

285
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.720
At first. don't uncover it.

286
00:34:02.360 --> 00:34:05.240
When the time comes. remove the bowl.

287
00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:07.560
Let there be light.

288
00:34:08.080 --> 00:34:10.280
At that moment.

289
00:34:10.360 --> 00:34:14.120
You will catch the spirit of "Etxejaun" off guard.

290
00:34:17.080 --> 00:34:21.760
Pierce a rooster's
heart with pins.

291
00:34:23.200 --> 00:34:26.600
and throws some rotten corn on the ground.

292
00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:32.720
Then recite the following.

293
00:34:33.440 --> 00:34:35.600
Remember it well:

294
00:34:36.760 --> 00:34:40.520
"Inguma. I'm not afraid of you.

295
00:34:41.280 --> 00:34:43.640
Gauargi. light of the night. is with me.

296
00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:46.120
There are stars in the sky.

297
00:34:46.720 --> 00:34:48.680
in the meadow. herbs.

298
00:34:48.760 --> 00:34:50.160
and on the coast. sand.

299
00:34:51.240 --> 00:34:54.480
Until you finish counting these.

300
00:34:54.560 --> 00:34:57.560
do not appear before me."

301
00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:15.040
The window.

302
00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:52.680
Damned wretch!

303
00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:55.880
How could you do this to me?

304
00:35:56.640 --> 00:36:00.080
You are a pig!

305
00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:01.960
Grandfather?

306
00:36:07.800 --> 00:36:09.440
Antton...

307
00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:13.400
Lazy idiot.

308
00:36:13.480 --> 00:36:16.320
You are useless.

309
00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:19.640
You have let your sister

310
00:36:19.720 --> 00:36:22.440
tarnish the family name.

311
00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:26.120
Leave her alone!

312
00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.560
Cowardly fool!

313
00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:36.520
Don't you know what he's done?

314
00:36:38.560 --> 00:36:39.880
Anton. the corn!

315
00:36:52.600 --> 00:36:55.040
Anton. say it now!

316
00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:56.920
Inguma. I'm not afraid of you.

317
00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:58.720
Gauargi is with me.

318
00:36:59.320 --> 00:37:01.560
There are stars in the sky.
in the fields.

319
00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:04.800
herbs. and on the coast. sand.

320
00:37:04.880 --> 00:37:07.200
Until you finish counting these.
do not appear before me.

321
00:37:20.600 --> 00:37:22.040
The window!

322
00:38:21.680 --> 00:38:26.040
...28. 29. 30. 31

323
00:38:26.240 --> 00:38:30.000
32. 33. 34.

324
00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:34.960
 35. 36. 37...

325
00:39:23.080 --> 00:39:24.920
After Maritxu's death. the priest ruled

326
00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:28.280
that she had been
possessed by a demon.

327
00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:33.680
by a demon drawn by sin
and the evil arts of the witch.

328
00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:40.960
Lord. help my poor daughter.

329
00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:42.840
My God.

330
00:39:44.200 --> 00:39:45.360
I didn't want to...

331
00:39:47.520 --> 00:39:49.560
...but Maritxu was very sick.

332
00:39:51.760 --> 00:39:54.520
So I went to the witch's house...

333
00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:58.760
...and I did what she asked of me.

334
00:40:00.920 --> 00:40:02.120
I didn't know.

335
00:40:03.280 --> 00:40:04.200
I didn't know.

336
00:40:09.160 --> 00:40:10.920
And he seemed like a demon.

337
00:40:14.520 --> 00:40:15.520
Maritxu...

338
00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:26.320
That's how it happened.

339
00:40:27.440 --> 00:40:30.560
That's how Eugenia
told me. in tears.

340
00:40:31.920 --> 00:40:37.240
What horrible sin could the little girl
possibly have committed to make
her grandfather hate her like that?

341
00:40:37.320 --> 00:40:39.480
- It's a lie.
- What's a lie?

342
00:40:39.560 --> 00:40:42.360
Maritxu never did anything wrong.

343
00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:44.080
What would you know!

344
00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:45.400
I knew her well.

345
00:40:47.120 --> 00:40:49.000
Maritxu was very sick.

346
00:40:49.080 --> 00:40:52.120
and that witch's remedies
aggravated the illness.

347
00:40:52.600 --> 00:40:54.880
Do you accuse Estertxi of being a witch?

348
00:40:55.560 --> 00:40:57.720
We knew Estertxi well.

349
00:40:58.680 --> 00:41:01.840
She helped the people of
the village in her own way.

350
00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:05.480
Those candle suckers
wanted to get rid of her

351
00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:08.000
and they took her to Urdazubi.

352
00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:11.560
Who told you that it
was Estertxi's fault?

353
00:41:11.640 --> 00:41:12.720
Your husband?

354
00:41:12.800 --> 00:41:14.560
Don Mateo said it.

355
00:41:14.640 --> 00:41:16.560
Estertxi was our friend.

356
00:41:16.640 --> 00:41:18.080
Just like Maritxu was yours.

357
00:41:32.640 --> 00:41:38.440
That vain priest and his
superior. the abbot of Urdazubi.

358
00:41:39.040 --> 00:41:41.440
always turning people against one another.

359
00:41:42.040 --> 00:41:45.560
Let them burn in that hell they preach!

360
00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:49.280
There has been no word
of Mateo for a week.

361
00:41:49.360 --> 00:41:51.880
Since he went crazy at mass.

362
00:41:53.120 --> 00:41:54.400
I know

363
00:41:55.440 --> 00:41:57.880
what really happened to Mateo.

364
00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:07.240
It's my turn.

365
00:42:08.560 --> 00:42:11.240
Pay attention - or off you go!

366
00:42:15.080 --> 00:42:19.640
Mateo was arrogant and hypocritical.

367
00:42:22.640 --> 00:42:24.400
He was obsessed.

368
00:42:25.840 --> 00:42:29.000
Obsessed with authority.

369
00:42:30.520 --> 00:42:32.880
But. above all. with hunting.

370
00:42:34.240 --> 00:42:36.160
He always
whistled like a txistu flute.

371
00:42:39.280 --> 00:42:41.040
He whistled at both his hunting dog

372
00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:44.240
and his parishioners alike.

373
00:42:46.080 --> 00:42:48.400
Hence his nickname:

374
00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:51.880
Mateo Txistu.

375
00:42:57.880 --> 00:43:01.040
Mateo disappeared a week ago.

376
00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:05.240
after the death of Maritxu.
after what happened in the church.

377
00:43:07.480 --> 00:43:10.200
Beloved daughter and sister.

378
00:43:11.680 --> 00:43:15.560
María Oiartzun has left
us in the bloom of her youth.

379
00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:20.680
The weakness of the flesh made her sick.

380
00:43:20.760 --> 00:43:24.120
the enemy that ravages this village.

381
00:43:24.960 --> 00:43:26.200
Nevertheless.

382
00:43:26.880 --> 00:43:29.120
God is merciful.

383
00:43:30.560 --> 00:43:31.720
He loves us.

384
00:43:32.800 --> 00:43:34.000
He holds us in esteem.

385
00:43:36.040 --> 00:43:40.600
Family and neighbours.
let us pray for her soul.

386
00:43:41.320 --> 00:43:45.400
for only thus will she
be spared the fires of hell.

387
00:43:49.240 --> 00:43:53.200
Grant them. Lord. eternal rest.

388
00:43:54.240 --> 00:43:57.040
and may the perpetual
light shine upon them.

389
00:43:58.400 --> 00:44:01.360
In Zion. may they sing your praises.

390
00:44:01.440 --> 00:44:05.000
In Jerusalem. the vow shall
be fulfilled to you.

391
00:44:06.320 --> 00:44:09.880
Hear my prayers.

392
00:44:09.960 --> 00:44:13.200
You. towards whom all mortals go.

393
00:44:14.240 --> 00:44:18.280
Grant them. Lord. eternal rest.

394
00:44:19.120 --> 00:44:22.320
and may the perpetual
light shine upon them.

395
00:44:27.800 --> 00:44:29.680
May she rest in peace.

396
00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:35.800
Amen.

397
00:44:45.760 --> 00:44:49.240
The whole village knew
of his love of hunting.

398
00:44:51.840 --> 00:44:57.280
He used to say that God had
given man the gift of hunting

399
00:44:57.360 --> 00:45:00.320
above all other creatures.

400
00:45:09.120 --> 00:45:11.520
I know it too well -

401
00:45:12.920 --> 00:45:15.200
I kept house for him.

402
00:45:16.120 --> 00:45:17.800
I helped him in the parish.

403
00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:47.680
Mateo was a very reserved man...

404
00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:53.360
...and he confided his obsessions

405
00:45:54.560 --> 00:45:57.760
only to the One he
believed was above him.

406
00:46:01.720 --> 00:46:06.720
I confess to Almighty God
and to you. my brothers.

407
00:46:06.800 --> 00:46:09.480
that I have greatly sinned in thought.

408
00:46:09.560 --> 00:46:13.600
word. deed and omission.

409
00:46:14.080 --> 00:46:15.360
Through my fault.

410
00:46:16.040 --> 00:46:17.240
Through my fault.

411
00:46:18.280 --> 00:46:21.600
Through my grievous fault.

412
00:46:30.400 --> 00:46:32.360
Lord. I have sinned.

413
00:46:34.320 --> 00:46:37.600
I have felt in my very flesh.
the tempter devil

414
00:46:37.680 --> 00:46:40.240
trying to lead me astray from Your path.

415
00:46:40.320 --> 00:46:42.160
Hear me. my Lord;

416
00:46:43.280 --> 00:46:46.920
and free me from this burden.

417
00:46:51.360 --> 00:46:56.240
This morning. I went hunting
with my faithful dog.

418
00:46:58.880 --> 00:47:02.720
Why has Your grace willed
that I should stumble

419
00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:07.840
upon the obstinate
blasphemy made flesh?

420
00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:21.000
He said what he saw there had
driven him to the brink of madness.

421
00:47:23.360 --> 00:47:24.280
Search!

422
00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.080
Come here!

423
00:47:45.160 --> 00:47:47.160
Search here!

424
00:48:39.120 --> 00:48:41.000
I could spend the whole day dancing.

425
00:48:43.600 --> 00:48:44.680
Give me your hand.

426
00:48:58.440 --> 00:49:00.920
It's more than Pello has ever given me.

427
00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:05.280
That fool doesn't know what he has at home.

428
00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:09.360
I can't stand it. And
the nights are the worst.

429
00:49:10.160 --> 00:49:14.320
You're lucky. With your widowed mother.
You can remain an old maid to help her.

430
00:49:15.160 --> 00:49:20.080
Lucky. yes. but...
"A mere girl. a bald head".

431
00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:23.440
I can't take it anymore.

432
00:49:24.160 --> 00:49:25.160
Well...

433
00:49:28.600 --> 00:49:29.960
...let's get out of here.

434
00:49:30.800 --> 00:49:32.000
To Bayonne.

435
00:49:32.960 --> 00:49:34.840
Let's leave tonight.

436
00:49:34.920 --> 00:49:36.080
Just the two of us.

437
00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:38.280
Are you crazy?

438
00:49:38.360 --> 00:49:40.360
Two women alone out there?

439
00:49:40.440 --> 00:49:43.000
If they catch us.
Pello will beat me senseless.

440
00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:48.320
Then we'll dress up as men.

441
00:49:48.400 --> 00:49:51.480
You take Pello's clothes.
and I'll take my brother's.

442
00:49:55.720 --> 00:49:57.120
If it were that easy...

443
00:50:04.240 --> 00:50:06.120
One of these days. we'll land
ourselves in hot water

444
00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:08.280
...and that'll be the end of it.

445
00:50:17.400 --> 00:50:18.400
I don't know.

446
00:50:19.120 --> 00:50:20.560
I don't know.
He's my husband.

447
00:50:42.760 --> 00:50:44.120
Hello beautiful.

448
00:50:44.800 --> 00:50:47.240
Do you want to marry me?

449
00:50:47.320 --> 00:50:48.200
No.

450
00:50:49.120 --> 00:50:53.320
I'm a little short-sighted.
but I have a fine dowry.

451
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:54.280
Look.

452
00:50:58.360 --> 00:51:01.900
Come on. darling - give me a kiss on the trout!

453
00:51:02.000 --> 00:51:03.020
- No!

454
00:51:03.580 --> 00:51:05.660
I'd sooner kiss a goat's ass!

455
00:51:05.740 --> 00:51:07.220
Witch!

456
00:51:08.660 --> 00:51:10.180
Come with me!

457
00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:28.900
With you. I'd go anywhere.

458
00:55:10.340 --> 00:55:15.940
Was what I saw real or
was it a trick of the devil?

459
00:55:17.620 --> 00:55:20.100
Should I tell the abbot?

460
00:55:46.020 --> 00:55:47.020
Father Mateo.

461
00:55:47.740 --> 00:55:49.300
Pello Goienetxea.

462
00:56:05.780 --> 00:56:06.620
Sit down.

463
00:56:12.460 --> 00:56:17.340
I have received your request to
work the apple orchard at the abbey.

464
00:56:18.580 --> 00:56:21.620
I have a bad leg. but I
would be a good foreman.

465
00:56:23.020 --> 00:56:28.020
I know the cider-making process
well. I worked for years at Hernani.

466
00:56:28.100 --> 00:56:29.140
I'm sure.

467
00:56:31.140 --> 00:56:33.340
But I called you for something else.

468
00:56:35.740 --> 00:56:40.380
I need you and your wife to
come with me to Urdazubi to

469
00:56:40.460 --> 00:56:45.780
declare before the judge that
Esther Barrenetxea is a witch.

470
00:56:48.500 --> 00:56:51.060
I wouldn't want to get
involved in those matters.

471
00:56:52.060 --> 00:56:52.980
Don't worry.

472
00:56:55.580 --> 00:56:58.020
I know you are a good Christian.

473
00:56:59.460 --> 00:57:02.940
And the Church knows
how to reward its good men.

474
00:57:06.140 --> 00:57:08.900
But I can't say the same about your wife.

475
00:57:10.540 --> 00:57:12.500
I have seen it with my own eyes.

476
00:57:52.660 --> 00:57:56.660
There are three enemies of our soul:

477
00:57:56.740 --> 00:58:01.820
the world. the devil and the flesh.

478
00:58:02.100 --> 00:58:06.940
And. of the three. the most dangerous -
 the gravest - is the flesh.

479
00:58:07.900 --> 00:58:10.420
The flesh is weak. but also strong.

480
00:58:11.420 --> 00:58:16.500
Weak to defend
and strong to tempt.

481
00:58:16.580 --> 00:58:18.580
Not even murder is so grave!

482
00:58:18.660 --> 00:58:23.100
For the sin of the
flesh rots the hearts of

483
00:58:23.180 --> 00:58:25.620
good Christians. as it spreads like a

484
00:58:25.700 --> 00:58:30.460
plague. thus condemning.
not only the souls of sinners.

485
00:58:30.980 --> 00:58:34.260
but the very pillars of our society.

486
00:58:37.100 --> 00:58:42.220
Witchcraft and indecency
lead our people to perdition.

487
00:58:42.580 --> 00:58:46.940
More and more women stray
from the path of the Lord

488
00:58:47.020 --> 00:58:50.220
and lose themselves on
the devil's road.

489
00:58:52.140 --> 00:58:53.620
And listen to me.

490
00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:59.220
The only way to
atone for carnal sins...

491
00:59:01.220 --> 00:59:03.340
...is by denouncing a witch.

492
00:59:09.340 --> 00:59:11.180
At the Urdazubi Abbey. we will have the

493
00:59:11.260 --> 00:59:16.060
honourable commissioner
of the Holy Inquisition.

494
00:59:17.180 --> 00:59:19.260
You must go to him

495
00:59:19.980 --> 00:59:26.420
if you suspect that a neighbour
may be linked to witchcraft.

496
00:59:28.180 --> 00:59:31.060
We have already received
several complaints.

497
00:59:33.980 --> 00:59:38.660
Whoever covers up a
witch is also an accomplice.

498
01:00:24.700 --> 01:00:26.220
Damn witch!

499
01:00:33.820 --> 01:00:35.660
It's you. witch!
I know!

500
01:00:36.580 --> 01:00:40.260
I'll follow you to
hell if I have to!

501
01:01:05.300 --> 01:01:06.420
Catch her!

502
01:01:30.980 --> 01:01:33.420
Nobody saw him again.

503
01:01:35.420 --> 01:01:39.660
But it is said that at night.
in the mountains.

504
01:01:39.740 --> 01:01:44.860
some have heard Mateo's whistles
calling to his dog.

505
01:01:46.260 --> 01:01:50.860
The priest is a restless soul

506
01:01:51.460 --> 01:01:55.060
and so he will continue

507
01:01:55.860 --> 01:01:58.880
wandering. cursed.
chasing the hare forever.

508
01:02:03.460 --> 01:02:05.660
That's not true.
How do you know that?

509
01:02:06.020 --> 01:02:07.580
You weren't there.

510
01:02:07.660 --> 01:02:10.580
The priest himself told
me before he disappeared.

511
01:02:10.660 --> 01:02:13.740
Enough pretending.
We know everything!

512
01:02:13.820 --> 01:02:18.100
He swore he would keep it secret
if I gave testimony.

513
01:02:18.180 --> 01:02:21.820
So you admit it - did you freely
sign the statement against Estertxi?

514
01:02:22.340 --> 01:02:23.540
No. I don't...

515
01:02:23.620 --> 01:02:24.900
"No" what?

516
01:02:24.980 --> 01:02:26.820
That they didn't force you?

517
01:02:26.900 --> 01:02:29.060
- Did you do it voluntarily?
- No!

518
01:02:29.140 --> 01:02:30.700
Tell the truth. stupid.

519
01:02:31.500 --> 01:02:36.580
The priest forced you to sign in exchange
for keeping quiet about what happened
between you and Maritxu.

520
01:02:36.660 --> 01:02:38.300
We know everything.

521
01:02:38.380 --> 01:02:41.740
They burned Estertxi because of you.

522
01:02:42.460 --> 01:02:43.620
What?

523
01:02:43.700 --> 01:02:46.460
Imagine how much she must
have suffered when they burned her.

524
01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:50.020
I... I didn't know...

525
01:02:50.100 --> 01:02:52.820
You're guilty - murderess!

526
01:02:52.900 --> 01:02:53.980
No!

527
01:02:54.060 --> 01:02:56.700
You too must
answer to the witches.

528
01:02:56.780 --> 01:02:59.820
What witches?
You are nothing more than crazy old women!

529
01:03:00.580 --> 01:03:02.460
You say we're not? Yes we are.

530
01:03:03.060 --> 01:03:05.220
Look how many we are - a thousand and one.

531
01:03:09.580 --> 01:03:13.540
You will come with us to the witches' sabbath.

532
01:03:16.940 --> 01:03:20.180
IV
THE SABBATH

533
01:03:33.500 --> 01:03:35.980
Pello!

534
01:03:37.860 --> 01:03:40.140
Open!
Please open!

535
01:03:40.940 --> 01:03:43.020
Let me in. for God's sake!

536
01:03:46.100 --> 01:03:47.500
Damn pig.

537
01:03:47.580 --> 01:03:50.660
- You. who wanted to poison me?
